package cajeta.xpu;

/**
 * A runtime device capability — a hardware feature the **active** device may or
 * may not advertise, queried with {@link Device#supports}. This is the model's
 * capability-heuristic input (cajeta-docs/gpu/CajetaGPU.md §1, RayQuery.md §6):
 * an app chooses a native fast path when the silicon has it, and falls back to
 * core (which floors to software) when it doesn't.
 *
 *     if (Device.supports(Capability.RayQueryNative)) {
 *         // build a hardware acceleration structure; OpRayQuery on the GPU
 *     } else {
 *         // the portable software BVH path — same source, runs anywhere
 *     }
 *
 * This is the RUNTIME counterpart of the compile-time capability *traits* in
 * {@link Capabilities} (template constraints resolved at codegen): traits gate
 * *which kernel* compiles for a target; `Capability` + `Device.supports` gate
 * *which path the host dispatches* at run time on the device it actually got.
 *
 * The ordinal is the **stable native contract** — `__cajeta_xpu_device_supports`
 * (runtime/native/cajeta_runtime.c) switches on it. Do not reorder; append only.
 *
 * v1 surfaces the capabilities with a crisp per-device answer and an immediate
 * consumer (the ray-query path choice). More land as the runtime grows the probes
 * (cooperative matrix, unified memory, the wave/atomic feature tiers) — append to
 * the end so the ordinals stay stable.
 */
public enum Capability {
    RayQueryNative,      // 0 — hardware INLINE ray query (VK_KHR_ray_query / equivalent)
    RayQueryRtCore,      // 1 — pipeline-based RT-core ray query (NVIDIA OptiX on CUDA)
    CoopMatrixBf16F32Acc,// 2 — a LAUNCHABLE bf16-operand / f32-accumulator
                         //     cooperative-matrix GEMM path on the active backend
                         //     (cajeta-llama 2.2.6). Launchable, not necessarily
                         //     native: CPU answers true (software tier runs the
                         //     mix); Vulkan answers false (no bf16 coop config —
                         //     the kernel is compile-skipped there); CUDA needs
                         //     sm_80+, HIP needs RDNA3+ (gfx11xx/gfx12xx).
    AtomicInt64          // 3 — Buffer<int64|uint64>.atomic* runs natively.
                         //     Vulkan reports the device's own
                         //     VK_KHR_shader_atomic_int64 verdict; neither
                         //     Apple driver advertises it, so both answer
                         //     false (apple-vulkan spec 4.6). CPU/CUDA/HIP
                         //     answer true.
}
